# TapMind SDK catalog (mobile)

Use this when editing changelog, package versions, glossary, or integration docs.

## SDK vs adapter

| Layer | Role |
| --- | --- |
| **SDK** (`TapMindSdk`) | TapMind core: server config, load/show ads (GMA/GAM under the hood), tracking, privacy, timeouts, fallback |
| **Adapter** (`customadapter-admob`, `customadapter-gam`, `customadapter-applovin`, `customadapter-ironsource`, etc.) | Mediation bridge: receives platform load request, calls TapMind SDK, returns loaded/failed/clicked to that platform |

Publishers integrate via mediation (AdMob, GAM, AppLovin MAX, LevelPlay), not TapMind directly. **SDK = logic. Adapter = plug for each mediation partner.**

## Three mobile products

| Product | Demand | Integration |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Custom Adapter GMA SDK** (CA-GMA) | Current GMA | Plugs into mediations via adapters |
| **Custom Adapter GMA Next-Gen SDK** (CA-NG) | Next-Gen GMA | Same adapter model, different GMA generation |
| **Orchestration SDK** | GMA | Standalone; no mediation adapters (defer unless asked) |

GMA vs Next-Gen: same mediation adapter pattern; only the GMA demand generation differs.

## What a "package" is

**Package** = **Framework/Native** + **Platform (Android/iOS)** + **Mediation (AdMob, GAM, AppLovin MAX, LevelPlay)**

Examples: Native Android AdMob, Flutter iOS GAM, Unity Android LevelPlay.

Supported frameworks: Native Android, Native iOS, Flutter, Unity, React Native, Cocos (each Android/iOS where applicable).

## Release and build order

### Native (Android / iOS)

1. New features land in the **platform SDK** first (separate SDK per platform: Native Android SDK, Native iOS SDK).
2. **Adapters** are add-ons on the same SDK - e.g. Native Android GAM after Native Android AdMob needs **adapter-only** work; SDK logic unchanged.
3. Same pattern on iOS.

### Wrapper frameworks (Flutter, Unity, RN, Cocos)

- Each wrapper bundles **Native adapter + Native SDK** for that platform/mediation.
- Typical flow: ship on Native Android/iOS first, then update wrapper packages.
- Example: feature in Native Android AdMob, publisher needs Flutter Android GAM → build **Native Android GAM** (SDK unchanged) → that bundle ships inside **Flutter Android GAM**.

## Docs site mapping

- **SDK Changelog** (`sdk-changelog/`): per product (CA-GMA, CA-NG; Orchestration when relevant).
- **Package Versions** (`package-versions.mdx`): CA-GMA and CA-NG only (Orchestration has no mediation packages).
- **Glossary**: CA-GMA / CA-NG abbreviations; Orchestration terms deferred.

When adding entries, respect native-first release order and wrapper "built on" native version relationships.
